{
  "id": 259702049,
  "iid": 12837,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Qt: remove use of qAsConst which is deprecated in Qt 6.6",
  "description": "The parameters passed to qAsConst are already of type `const T&`, so we\ndo not need `qAsConst`. Remove it to address deprecation warnings.\n\nSee also https://www.kdab.com/blog-qasconst-and-stdas_const/\n___\nTested with Qt 5 and Qt 6 (qt5-base 5.15.11+kde+r138-1, qt6-base 6.6.0-2 on Arch Linux).\n\nFor easier verification, here are the matches in origin/master (and origin/release-4.2):\n```cpp\n// ui/qt/follow_stream_dialog.cpp\nvoid FollowStreamDialog::addCodecs(const QMap<QString, QTextCodec *> &codecMap)\n{\n    // ...\n    for (const auto &codec : qAsConst(codecMap)) {\n\n// ui/qt/models/packet_list_model.cpp\nvoid PacketListModel::addFrameComment(const QModelIndexList &indices, const QByteArray &comment)\n{\n    // ...\n    for (const auto &index : qAsConst(indices)) {\n\nvoid PacketListModel::deleteFrameComments(const QModelIndexList &indices)\n{\n    // ...\n    for (const auto &index : qAsConst(indices)) {\n\n// ui/qt/show_packet_bytes_dialog.cpp\nvoid ShowPacketBytesDialog::addCodecs(const QMap<QString, QTextCodec *> &codecMap)\n{\n    // ...\n    for (const auto &codec : qAsConst(codecMap)) {\n```\n\nThe release-4.0 branch also has two matches in `follow_stream_dialog.cpp` and `show_packet_bytes_dialog.cpp` with the same issue/fix. Probably not worth fixing though since this only affects Qt 6.6 and newer?\n\nFixes !9844 (for packet_list_model.cpp, @nicolas17) and commit 9fc054a65bfadf40325bb4f5185c7247ed4a9a6c (for the other two, @johnthacker).\nI need extra eyes on whether it is okay to drop `qAsConst` for the `QMap`s given that their values are non-const. I think it is okay, but just to be sure...",
