    {
      "id": "00bebaee2af9b7e62371f2889e004f8ebe94336a",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1622251733,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> whether it is okay to drop qAsConst for the QMaps given that their values are non-const.\n\nI think that if the QMap is not const a detach can still occur. I believe the reason that `qAsConst` is deprecated in Qt 6.6 is because Qt 6.x requires C++17, C++17 provides `std::as_const` and they have decided it's time to move people to the C++17 standard version, similar to what was previously done with `qMove()` and `std::move`. https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/qtglobal-obsolete.html\n\nHowever, as long as we support Qt5 we don't require C++17, and we can fail compilation with `std::as_const` on some supported platforms.\n\nWe could test `QT_VERSION_CHECK` and use `std::as_const` on later versions.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-10-27T11:36:55.282Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-10-27T11:36:55.282Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 259702049,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 12837,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
