    {
      "id": "15939b3b6d818d139554bad3c127d1b00e24e12a",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1622706004,
          "type": null,
          "body": "The `QMap`s themselves are already `const` references, so detaching should not occur according to the linked KDAB article:\n```c++\nvoid FollowStreamDialog::addCodecs(const QMap<QString, QTextCodec *> &codecMap)\nvoid ShowPacketBytesDialog::addCodecs(const QMap<QString, QTextCodec *> &codecMap)\n```\n\nThe value of the map is a pointer, `QTextCodec *`, so we should not be concerned about copy constructors and so on right?\n\nI don't think `qAsConst` or `std::as_const` will add much. In the [QMap](https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/qmap.html) documentation, they suggest `std::as_const` as the map is non-const:\n```c++\nQMap<QString, int> map;\n...\nfor (int value : std::as_const(map))\n    cout << value << endl;\n```",
          "author": {
            "id": 2415432,
            "username": "Lekensteyn",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Peter Wu",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/efcf30db53f30b15e7c905ef37bd4dc44d87573bd92baf97cd707115d3fcd0c0?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/Lekensteyn"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-10-27T13:05:24.812Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-10-27T13:06:42.684Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 259702049,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 12837,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
